// Copyright (c) 2026 Roshan. All rights reserved.// Proprietary license — see LICENSE file for details.package com.roshan.persona.productivity.noteimport androidx.room.ColumnInfoimport androidx.room.Entityimport androidx.room.Fts4import androidx.room.PrimaryKey/** * NOUS — Note Room Entity (Module 14 v1.2 — Step 14.3). * * Production-ready Room entity for the `notes` table. * * ## Schema * * | Column | Type | Notes | * |--------|------|-------| * | id | TEXT (PK) | UUID-style note ID | * | title | TEXT | Plain-text title (searchable) | * | body_iv | TEXT | Base64 IV for AES-GCM body decryption | * | body_ciphertext | TEXT | Base64 ciphertext of note body | * | plain_text_body | TEXT | Markdown-stripped body (for FTS sync) | * | content_type | TEXT | enum name: TEXT/MARKDOWN/CODE/LIST | * | tags | TEXT | comma-separated tag list | * | created_at_ms | INTEGER | epoch ms | * | updated_at_ms | INTEGER | epoch ms | * * ## Encryption * * The note body is stored as `body_iv` + `body_ciphertext` (AES-256-GCM via * [NoteEncryptionHelper]). The plaintext body NEVER appears in this table. * * The `plain_text_body` column holds the markdown-stripped body for syncing * to [NoteFtsEntity] (the FTS5 virtual table). In production this lives in * a SQLCipher-encrypted DB file, so search text is still protected at the * file-system level even though it isn't field-level encrypted. * * ## v1 Usage * * This entity is the production-ready Room contract. In v1, [NoteEngine] * uses the in-memory [NoteStore] for actual persistence (sufficient for * unit tests + smoke testing). When the production Room DB is wired (post- * Module 12 SqlCipherMigration), [NoteEngine] switches to use [NoteDao]. */@Entity(tableName = "notes")data class NoteEntity(    @PrimaryKey    @ColumnInfo(name = "id")    val id: String,    @ColumnInfo(name = "title")    val title: String,    @ColumnInfo(name = "body_iv")    val bodyIv: String?,    @ColumnInfo(name = "body_ciphertext")    val bodyCiphertext: String?,    @ColumnInfo(name = "plain_text_body")    val plainTextBody: String,    @ColumnInfo(name = "content_type")    val contentType: String,    @ColumnInfo(name = "tags")    val tags: String,  // comma-separated    @ColumnInfo(name = "created_at_ms")    val createdAtMs: Long,    @ColumnInfo(name = "updated_at_ms")    val updatedAtMs: Long,)/** * NOUS — Note FTS5 Search Index (Module 14 v1.2 — Step 14.3). * * Room's `@Fts4` annotation creates a SQLite FTS4 virtual table. We use FTS4 * (instead of FTS5) because Room's annotation processor natively supports it * and FTS4 is sufficient for our search needs (phrase search + prefix search). * * For FTS5-specific features (e.g., BM25 ranking), a raw-SQL approach with * `CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE notes_fts USING fts5(...)` can be added later via * a Room migration. The current @Fts4 setup gives us MATCH-based search * with prefix queries (`med*` matches `medicine`). * * ## Syncing * * The FTS table is kept in sync with the `notes` table via triggers (auto- * generated by Room when `contentEntity` is set). When a note is inserted / * updated / deleted in [NoteEntity], Room auto-syncs the FTS index. * * ## Query Sanitization * * All user-supplied search queries are sanitized via * [com.roshan.persona.productivity.alarm.Fts5Utils.escapeFts5Query] before * being passed to `MATCH`. This prevents FTS5 operator injection (e.g., a * user searching for `*` or `:` would otherwise break the query). */@Fts4(contentEntity = NoteEntity::class)@Entity(tableName = "notes_fts")data class NoteFtsEntity(    @ColumnInfo(name = "title")    val title: String,    @ColumnInfo(name = "plain_text_body")    val plainTextBody: String,)